# Tailwind Class Order

When writing or editing `className`, `class`, or `cn()` arguments, order utility classes in this sequence:

1. **Element** — classes that apply directly to the element itself (custom utilities, typography, cursor, pointer-events, transitions on self)
2. **Margin & padding** — `m-*`, `p-*`, and axis variants
3. **Width & height** — `w-*`, `h-*`, `min-*`, `max-*`, `size-*`, `aspect-*`
4. **Position & layout** — positioning, stacking, overflow, display on the element (not flex/grid children)
5. **Color** — background, text, fill, stroke, gradients, opacity
6. **Border** — border, outline, ring, divide
7. **Rounding** — `rounded-*`
8. **Shadow** — `shadow-*`
9. **Children (flex & grid)** — flex/grid display, alignment, gap, order

Separate groups with a single space. Keep variant prefixes (`hover:`, `md:`, `dark:`) attached to each utility.

## Group Reference

| Group | Examples |
|-------|----------|
| Element | `shrink-*`, `grow-*`, `font-*`, `truncate`, `whitespace-*`, `cursor-*`, `select-*`, `pointer-events-*`, `transition-*`, `duration-*`, `animate-*` |
| Margin & padding | `m-*`, `mx-*`, `my-*`, `mt-*`, `mr-*`, `mb-*`, `ml-*`, `p-*`, `px-*`, `py-*`, `pt-*`, `pr-*`, `pb-*`, `pl-*` |
| Width & height | `w-*`, `h-*`, `min-w-*`, `max-w-*`, `min-h-*`, `max-h-*`, `size-*`, `aspect-*` |
| Position & layout | `relative`, `absolute`, `fixed`, `sticky`, `static`, `inset-*`, `top-*`, `right-*`, `bottom-*`, `left-*`, `z-*`, `overflow-*`, `block`, `inline`, `hidden`, `visible` |
| Color | `bg-*`, `text-*`, `fill-*`, `stroke-*`, `from-*`, `to-*`, `via-*`, `opacity-*` |
| Border | `border`, `border-*`, `outline-*`, `ring-*`, `divide-*` |
| Rounding | `rounded-*` |
| Shadow | `shadow-*` |
| Children | `flex`, `grid`, `inline-flex`, `flex-*`, `grid-*`, `gap-*`, `items-*`, `justify-*`, `content-*`, `self-*`, `place-*`, `order-*`, `col-*`, `row-*`, `space-x-*`, `space-y-*` |

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — groups mixed
<div className="flex gap-4 bg-muted p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm text-sm w-full border font-condensed" />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="p-4 w-full bg-muted text-sm font-condensed border rounded-lg shadow-sm flex gap-4" />
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="items-center justify-center hover:bg-primary flex h-9 px-4 rounded-md border bg-background shadow-xs" />

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="px-4 h-9 bg-background hover:bg-primary border rounded-md shadow-xs flex items-center justify-center" />
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — element utility after spacing
<div className="p-4 shrink-0 w-full flex" />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="shrink-0 p-4 w-full flex" />
```

When refactoring existing classes, reorder to match this sequence without changing behavior.
